[l_english.STATE_LORE_668]
Hoof City, a second-tier city on the southeast coast of Equestria, was once known for its elegant civic life and orderly streets. A sub-organization of the former Equestria Games once wanted to hold a rodeo here, but the event was forced to stop when rolling barrels nearly injured some onlookers. Since then, the city has banned many “barbaric” sports and has preferred more “elegant” activities such as golf, flower viewing, or afternoon tea. Even after the Empire took over, these habits remained unchanged; even when shivering in the cold wind, they would take off their warm hats to greet passing friends.
However, everything changed when a resistance force retreating from the Kingdom of Thicket, settled here. At first, the citizens complained about these uninvited guests — their chaos disrupted the city’s original elegant rhythm, and various “suspicious” gatherings suddenly appeared in the streets and alleys, making conversations in bakeries cautious. The city council reported these “troublemakers” to the Empire multiple times, but it is easy to imagine that the council’s response was always like: “The Canterlot EEMO thanks you for your report! The Imperial Army is on its way to the area; please remain patient and loyal! You may also choose to maintain city order yourself: see it, say it, sort it!”
Ironically, it was this resistance movement, viewed by the townsfolk as “chaotic”, that injected unprecedented vitality into Hoof City. Under the “coercion” of the former Lord of Chaos, gentlemen accustomed to playing golf now played buckball with soldiers from the central Equestria; ladies who only wanted to drink rose hip green tea and admire flowers in the afternoon began to play treasure hunt games with singing ginseng; the city council elders no longer locked themselves in their bedrooms reading newspapers while smoking pipes, reluctantly learning the board game “Ogres & Oubliettes” and becoming obsessed with it. They even revived the long-discontinued rodeo, making lassoing, barrel rolling, horse racing, and shooting popular again. Homeless creatures who once roamed the streets moved into newly built Fluttershy’s Animal Sanctuary; the restaurants of Hoof City were no longer filled with Octavia’s cello solos, but with the revelry of jazz bands in bars and rubber chickens at parties. The city’s temperature began to rise, and the shouts and laughter on the streets increased, the energetic fellas of the resistance made the factory machines run more efficiently, and the once lifeless city began to rejuvenate.
Nopony knows when one day, after Fancy Pants finishes his paperwork and takes off his monocle, he will remember that the quiet and loyal Hoof City in eastern Equestria seems to have not written to Canterlot for a long time.

[l_simp_chinese.STATE_LORE_668]
马蹄城，这座小马利亚东南沿海的二线城市，曾经以其优雅的市民生活和井然有序的街道而闻名。曾经小马利亚大赛的一个子组织想在这里举办一场牛仔大赛，但因为滚动的木桶险些伤到围观的小马，大赛也被迫终止。从那以后，这座城市便禁止了许多“野蛮”的运动，更加偏好那些“优雅”的活动，比如高尔夫球、赏花、或是喝下午茶。即使是帝国接管之后，这些习惯都未曾改变；即使有时在寒风中冻得瑟瑟发抖，他们也要脱下那御寒的帽子向路过的朋友行礼致敬。
然而，自从那支从灌丛谷王国撤退而来的抵抗军在这里落脚后，一切都改变了。起初，市民们对这些不速之客怨声载道 —— 他们的混乱打破了城市原有的优雅节奏，街头巷尾突然出现了各种“可疑”的集会，连面包店里的对话都变得小心翼翼起来。市议会曾经多次向帝国报告这些“麻烦分子”，但不用想象也可以知道，市议会每次得到的回复都是：“坎特洛特小马利亚帝国秩序部感谢您的举报！帝国军队已在前往该地区路上，请保持耐心与忠诚！您也可以选择自行维护城市秩序：看见，说出，解决！”
然而讽刺的是，正是这种被小市民们视为“混乱”的抵抗运动，却为马蹄城注入了前所未有的活力。在混沌领主的“逼迫”下，那些习惯于打高尔夫的绅士们现在与从中部来的抵抗军士兵们一起比赛后蹄球；那些只想要在午后喝着玫瑰果绿茶赏花的贵妇们开始与会唱歌的人参茶一起进行藏宝游戏；市议会的老爷们也不再抽着烟斗将自己关在卧室里阅读报纸，不情不愿地学习了《巨魔与地牢》桌游并随之变得沉迷其中。他们甚至恢复了当年停办的牛仔大赛，套圈、滚筒、赛马与射击变得再度流行起来。原本露宿街头无家可归的生物们住进了新建的柔柔可爱动物收养所；充斥马蹄城餐馆的不再是奥塔薇娅的大提琴独奏，而是酒吧中的爵士乐队与派对中的橡胶鸡交织在一起的狂欢。城市的温度开始上升，街道上的叫卖与欢笑声也越来越多，抵抗军那些精力充沛的小伙们让工厂的机器运转更有效率，原本死气沉沉的城市开始焕发出新的生机。
也不知到什么时候，当花花短裤又一次处理完公文，摘下单片镜的时候，他才会想起来，帝国东部那个安静而忠诚的马蹄城，似乎很久没有给坎特洛特写过信了。
